1795186314075145	sippycup-2u2m2v	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-30l	{"body":"2026-11-20: three of the five now have tests on this machine. (1) IPv6 gateway: tests/gateway.rs gives the throwaway namespace 2001:db8::10/64 with gateway 2001:db8::1; approved, the gateway does not arrive at a [::] listener; with a pasta that drops --map-host-loopback it arrives from [::1] (control); unapproved it is rejected and counted. Found on the way: a rejected IPv6 TCP connect fails with 'Permission denied', not 'No route to host'; docs corrected. (2) SCM_RIGHTS: sockets.rs the_peer_of_an_exposed_socket_can_pass_a_host_network_socket pins the documented open path (a UDP socket passed over an exposed socket sends to the host loopback; unexposed, connect is refused). (3) Real X server: sockets.rs display_works_with_a_real_x_server_and_is_off_by_default starts a private Xvnc (-displayfd, Unix sockets only, cookie in the runtime directory) and runs xdotool inside, with and without Landlock; skipped where Xvnc or xdotool is missing. STILL UNTESTED, both need root or another machine: (a) AppArmor: this kernel has no AppArmor LSM (lsm=capability,landlock,lockdown,yama,bpf), so neither the failure message nor the profile in DESIGN.md can be tried; needs an Ubuntu 24.04+ box or VM. (b) TIOCSTI: dev.tty.legacy_tiocsti is 0 and is a global sysctl (root to change), so the new-session layer is still shown only by /dev/tty being unavailable; needs a kernel with the setting 1 or older than 6.2."}	blake3:ZgMbmu6TiPorwos-MLIDGup6RiEP4HA4pxPOI9ML1fA
