1795199391875007	codex	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-1th	{"field":"description","value":"Deadline::passed combines wall and monotonic time, PassWatch::judge processes pass changes, and the parent and namespace init implement rechecks, termination grace, and heartbeat loss. Existing tests cover individual decisions and selected live timelines. Verify their composition against the revocation promise in docs/DESIGN.md.\n\nDrive production decisions with explicit clock readings and bounded event sequences. Cover exact expiry, wall-clock movement in either direction, delayed polls, edits or revocation around startup, and a delayed parent. Verify that the original deadline stays binding, a terminal decision cannot revert, and repeated input cannot restart termination grace. Include witnesses for continued execution of a valid pass, clean natural exit, and enforcement. A temporary strict-versus-inclusive boundary mutation must fail. Publish the event bound and scheduling assumptions. Exercise the same Rust decisions production uses. Report separately which guarantees assume a scheduled parent, a responsive init, and a particular clock. Record the command, the explored event bound, and both continued and terminated witnesses. Native integration and documentation of the public promise belong to bn-1ms. Clock reference: https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/clock_gettime.2.html"}	blake3:HMCtkThupNFYMsHepGOW3vojNu2UjV0sVIRLmZpyPpI
