1795199392398169	codex	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-24o	{"field":"title","value":"Surface missing explicitly requested hide paths"}	blake3:UMyM8XJjFRoeCWy-jKmilClnluoYYhx70dLavjMfyVs
1795199392400964	codex	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-24o	{"field":"description","value":"Seen in the 2026-11-20 review. spec.md documents 'A path that does not exist is ignored', and src/sandbox.rs hide_path returns Ok for a missing path or a dangling symlink, with no message. A mistyped --hide therefore hides nothing and the run looks the same (verified: playpen run --no-network --hide /nonexistent-zz -- true exits 0 with the normal header). With Landlock this cannot open a socket (all host sockets are refused anyway), but --hide is also used for files, and under --without-landlock for sockets outside the hidden directories. Stricter choices: refuse to start (exit 2) or print a note in the header. Left for the owner because the current behaviour is documented and scripts may rely on hiding optional paths.\n\nRetain the documented optional-path behavior by default and surface the missed explicit hide on the existing diagnostic channel, keeping command stdout usable. If a breaking refusal is proposed, obtain a separate compatibility decision. Test a missing explicit path, a dangling link and an existing path through the CLI. Distinguish explicitly requested hides from optional built-in paths and update docs/spec.md with the result."}	blake3:la-dAVspPK7fL9wJeTjTwp3_nzBxRe1kCZHWgXc0GnQ
